theorem a-congruence-chain-opening-with-an-equation
  note        The chain's first term a·f(a) is an integer beside f(a)·a in
              the equation its first link cites, which the requires line
              says is one; the build reads it so, and not from H4, which
              the step does not name.
  let a ∈ ℤ                                                           (H1)
  let b ∈ ℤ                                                           (H2)
  let n ∈ ℕ                                                           (H3)
  let f : ℤ → ℝ                                                       (H4)
  assume f(a) ∈ ℤ                                                     (H5)
  assume f(a)·a ≡ b (mod n)                                           (H6)
  assume b ≡ 1 (mod n)                                                (H7)
  then a·f(a) ≡ 1 (mod n)

1.  a·f(a) = f(a)·a
    algebra, from H5

2.  a·f(a) ≡ 1 (mod n)
    calculation
      a·f(a) = f(a)·a       1
             ≡ b (mod n)    H6
             ≡ 1 (mod n)    H7
    requires f(a)·a ∈ ℤ: membership, from H5
